  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed ground-floor flat, by reason of its constrained layout and reliance on a restricted internal lightwell to serve the primary bedrooms, would fail to provide an acceptable standard of accommodation in respect of natural light, outlook and ventilation. The absence of private external amenity space for the upper-floor flats would further contribute to an unsatisfactory standard of accommodation within an over-intensive development of a constrained site. The proposal would therefore fail to provide high-quality, functional accommodation for future occupiers, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The proposed development would result in the unjustified loss of approximately 37 square metres of basement floorspace currently serving the ground-floor commercial unit. In the absence of robust evidence, including appropriate marketing or commercial justification, to demonstrate that there is no ongoing need for this space to support the viability or operation of the Class E use, the proposal fails to safeguard local employment and commercial provision, contrary to Policy DM17 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012, Policy SD6 of the London Plan 2021 and paragraph 85 of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "The applicant has failed to submit a site-specific Flood Risk Assessment or Surface Water Drainage Strategy. In the absence of this information, the Local Planning Authority is unable to determine whether the development would appropriately manage surface water runoff or avoid increasing flood risk on or off site. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policies SI 12 and SI 13, Policy DM4 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012 and paragraph 182 of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "The application has not been accompanied by a completed Statutory Biodiversity Metric, including the Small Sites Metric where appropriate, or sufficient supporting information to demonstrate whether the development is exempt from mandatory Biodiversity Net Gain requirements or, if not exempt, how the required 10% Biodiversity Net Gain would be achieved. The proposal therefore fails to demonstrate that biodiversity impacts would be appropriately assessed, mitigated and compensated, contrary to Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, Policy G6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM6 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012.",
    "In the absence of an arboricultural survey, Arboricultural Impact Assessment and Arboricultural Method Statement prepared in accordance with BS5837:2012, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposed development would avoid unacceptable harm to trees within the site, including trees protected by virtue of their location within the Liverpool Road Conservation Area. The proposal therefore fails to demonstrate that it would adequately protect existing trees or preserve the character and appearance of the conservation area, contrary to London Plan Policy G7 and Policies CS8, DM6 and DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that adequate refuse and recycling storage can be accommodated and safely serviced within this constrained mid-terrace site without obstructing access routes or resulting in unsatisfactory living conditions for future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012 and the Sutton and Kingston Waste Technical Guidance 2021."
  ],
